From fbd63a0ebeb3ffceca7ae06392635ca2b1c68bb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:34:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 179/181] hydra: world shader from a material bound to the dome
 (K-119)

A material bound to a dome light becomes Cycles' world shader: its surface,
when it has one, replaces the dome's colour, texture or Karma sky; its volume
is the world volume. A dome without a bound material, or bound to a
volume-only material, keeps the shader it builds from its parameters. The
material's network is translated by HdCyclesMaterial::BuildWorldGraph, and a
material that syncs rebuilds the domes bound to it.

A Karma Sky Atmosphere gets a default world volume from its own
coefficients: Rayleigh and Mie scattering (Mie absorption, miephase as the
Henyey-Greenstein anisotropy), each thinning with the altitude over Karma's
planet by its scale height.

kernel: a world volume that varies in space ends at its octree's bounds
(+-10 km around the origin). Past them Cycles traced on at the root's
majorant to the ray's end, FLT_MAX for a ray that escapes: null collisions
without end, a GPU hang.
